# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite these to
# CRLF. That breaks two things: bash refuses scripts with \r line endings when
# they run in WSL, and ansible-vault can fail to decrypt a vault whose bytes were
# altered. Pin the line endings so a clone on any OS behaves identically.

*.sh          text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.j2          text eol=lf

# Encrypted Ansible Vault files: never apply EOL conversion or text diffing.
**/vault.yml  -text
